# Commits that changed formatting only, and that `git blame` should look through.
#
# This file is inert until the clone is told to read it:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# That setting is per-clone and cannot be committed, which is why the command is
# also in `AGENTS.md` and in `scripts/bootstrap-worktree.sh`. Without it every SHA
# below is ignored by nothing and `git blame` still reports the reformat.
#
# The setting is per-clone and this file is per-branch, and git calls a missing
# ignore list fatal rather than empty. So while branches cut before this file
# existed are still around, `git blame` on one of them dies with `could not open
# object name list`. Unset the config until you are back on a branch that has the
# file, or merge forward; the window closes once this reaches `main`.
#
# Add a commit here only when it changed no behaviour at all. A commit that mixes
# a reformat with a real edit makes the real edit unblameable, so keep them apart.

# style(ox): reformat to the repository's Biome settings
#
# `stacks/ox-alpha/` had never been checked by Biome 2.5.x. This commit ran the
# formatter and the `organizeImports` assist across 96 files — quote style double
# to single, line width 100 to 120, import order — and changed nothing else. The
# linter was held off so that no safe lint fix could slip a code change in beside
# the formatting. See `docs/adrs/0051-absorb-ox-into-the-shared-lint-gate.md`.
